# Inactive v2 capacity admission SQL — 3 November 2026, America/Toronto

New owned file only: `docs/pilot/conversation/sql-drafts/p5-voice-v2-capacity.sql`. Base connected main is `491f7f0caba6fd5b0bbd19c52126c37600170559`. Read AGENTS, latest continuation/P5 checkpoint, lifetime-change contract, completed v2 proof/cleanup and old admission/capacity dependencies. No prior source, SQL, schema, grants, migration journal, settings or runtime route was edited.

## Contract

Two service-only endpoints accept one exact `p_proof` JSON body, the unchanged twelve-field protocol-2 proof registration receipt: `bfa_p5_v2_capacity_claim` requires operation claim; `bfa_p5_v2_voice_inspect` requires inspect. Both return exact `{protocol:2, proof:<original body>, status:'claimed'|'denied'|'closed'}`. Strict shape, canonical nonnil identifiers, safe integer timing, full claim and bounded proof intervals are validated before writes. Malformed or endpoint-operation-mismatched requests raise `Unavailable`. The full response does not establish current Auth, service provenance or provider dispatch permission.

Private helpers live in the existing `bfa_p5_voice_v2` namespace; no table/schema/accounting copy is added. Parsing does not register or authenticate a proof. After common owner and namespaced receipt locks, `take_proof` requires an existing unconsumed protocol-2 row equal to the complete parsed candidate composite, including full claim, cleanup, Auth/version/fingerprint and every original timestamp. Missing, already-consumed, foreign, legacy or changed tuples deny without consuming or performing negative cleanup work.

An exact proof is consumed once before semantic admission checks. The first clock sample is bounded and checked against the retained owner high-water. A safe normal sample advances that high-water so a later sample cannot hide a rollback between consumption and eligibility. A safe rollback burns the receipt and denies without lowering the clock. An unavailable/out-of-range initial sample writes consumed_ms=0 as an explicit non-null unknown-time consumption fence and immediately denies. Zero is never Auth freshness or a claimed consumption timestamp. Original verified/identity/proof/effective times remain unchanged. The local selected composite deliberately retains consumed_ms NULL while the persistent row is consumed; only that original composite enters the completed v2 eligibility predicate. SQL exceptions or outer transaction rollback remain uncertainty, not a guaranteed committed burn. The unchanged clock function is nonnull in normal operation; a later artificial NULL passed into legacy observe_now may raise and roll back.

`current` calls only the completed v2 eligibility helper. It requires current exact parent/no retained legacy fence, issuance association, protocol-2 cleanup, current thread/generation/allowlist/approval, claim/winner and safe post-lock time. Its exact negative deadline and terminal behavior remains intact. Missing/revoked parent, legacy fence or missing protected records deny without inventing Auth revocation.

One private capacity-admit path composes this into combined claim and existing-claim-only inspect. New claim atomically inserts the attempt winner, debits the existing quota once, inserts the shared claim/allocation and increments pool occupied/cumulative held units. A base-only claim is refused; no lazy attachment exists. Inspect cannot insert or debit. Exact existing capacity observations may succeed at the slot/unit limit with zero remaining quota, because their original reservation already committed. Current disabled/quarantined/over-limit pool, quota unit mismatch, wrong route, rebound approval quota policy or conflicting allocation denies. Existing quota/pool association is checked before selecting a different quota or locking a route pool, so later retirement cannot acquire a second pool in inverted order. Version changes alone are left to the future expected-version capacity mark.

After quota/route/pool locks, current v2 eligibility and original proof time are checked again before positive return or new accounting. Three normal clock samples occur: consumption, initial eligibility, final eligibility. Administrative routes/provisioning remain outside this implementation; native contention and actual Auth serialization remain unproven.

The narrow versioned retirement helper requires exact protocol-2 cleanup/Auth/full claim and matching retained claim/allocation owner, cleanup, attempt and units. It then uses the existing quota/pool and requires a nonzero occupied counter before releasing an exact terminal unmarked slot. Missing/inconsistent records deny retirement. Cumulative held units and quota are never refunded. Marked uncertain operations can become closed while their slot remains held until whole-operation finality reaches the unchanged exact reconciliation boundary. A parent failure alone does not manufacture a terminal cleanup or free a slot.

Only new function privileges are revoked/granted in their creation transaction. Existing close/reconcile, all old enabling functions and their grants remain unchanged. Consequently this is inactive, nondeployable preparation until versioned capacity mark/orchestration and quiesced no-fallback cutover are completed. No real Auth/provider calls, activation, publication or Lovable paid edit occurred.

## Review and validation

Self-review and independent/root review corrected two design details before the first actual SQL run: recording the consumption sample in the shared high-water, and checking existing quota/route identity before shared-pool acquisition. The narrow exact retirement helper also guards cleanup association and counter underflow. No prior source was modified. Independent source review found no remaining blocker at the final hash below.

The SQL test owner reports the first completed actual PostgreSQL/PGlite run passed 69/69; no initial SQL implementation failure occurred. Root reconciliation of that agent's completed evidence: the expanded final frozen suite passes 77/77, including rollback/route regressions, at the unchanged SQL hash below. An intermediate 76/77 result came from a retired-attempt fixture violating the unchanged retired/winner CHECK; its JSON diagnostic and the corrected valid fixture are recorded in sql-test-notes.md and the combined evidence. Root owns aggregate tests, strict TypeScript, scoped lint and production build. These are fictional Auth/approval records, controlled time, sequential committed-state checks and local transport doubles, not native multi-connection scheduling, real HTTP/Auth/provider or device acceptance. No exact-once external create claim is made.

