# Independent review — isolated v2 capacity admission

Reviewed 3 November 2026, America/Toronto, on baseline connected main `491f7f0caba6fd5b0bbd19c52126c37600170559`. This is offline source and fictional test evidence, not deployment, native PostgreSQL concurrency, deployed Auth or provider/device acceptance.

## Scope and status

Read AGENTS, current continuation marker, lifetime-change contract, prior v26 independent review, complete v2 proof eligibility/registration, legacy capacity/admission and the actual legacy store caller mapping. The bounded new path must compose locked single-use v2 proof consumption directly into shared atomic capacity admission and existing-capacity-only inspection; no separate base-claim implementation is needed. Capacity mark, host orchestration and quiesced no-fallback cutover remain deferred.

No remaining source blocker found in the complete new SQL and strict transport at the hashes below. Re-read the monotonic high-water and early exact quota/route guards after their final changes. Root owns final aggregate validation; the SQL test owner owns actual SQL execution evidence.

## Transport checks

The new mapping requires the complete exact twelve-field protocol-2 proof and enforces claim/inspect operation before the one captured protected RPC call. Input and output use own enumerable data fields, lowercase nonnil identities, safe integer timing, immutable full claim/Auth/cleanup association and positive receipt interval at most 30000 ms. Parsing detaches values, nested objects are frozen and every echoed identity and timing value must match. Null, old/minimal acknowledgment shapes, unsupported status/protocol and mismatched replies reject. Errors are sanitized. No clock, Auth SDK, credential/client creation, retries, fallback, runtime route or provider exists.

The success shape `{protocol:2,proof,status}` deliberately differs from v1 `{claim,state}`. Shape/provenance checks do not authenticate a transport, establish current request-bound Auth or provide dispatch authority. Denied/lost/malformed replies can follow committed proof consumption or negative/retained capacity evidence; they do not prove rollback or authorize replacement identities. Existing claims must not require or spend a second quota reservation.

