Added exactly two cases in `p5-voice-v2-capacity-review.test.ts`. Both compose the actual new transport with the unchanged v1 admission bridge through deliberately fictional old registration/claim ports. One reaches claim acknowledgment; the other reaches the mandatory immediate post-claim inspect. Even a matched protocol-2 `claimed` reply cannot activate the old bridge, and its retained exact cleanup closes once. The test conversion is only a fixture and installs no application adapter. These cases establish acknowledgment separation, not SQL admission or provider permission.

